Absence seizures
       Adult initially 500 mg daily in 2 divided doses, increased by 250 mg every 5–7 days to usual dose of 1–1.5 g daily in 2 divided doses;
       occasionally up to 2 g daily may be needed

Cystic fibrosis with at least 1 eligible mutation of the CFTR gene (see New Zealand Medicine Data Sheet
 for eligible mutations)
    Oral
       Adult 150 mg every 12 hours
 Note Reduce dose to 150 mg twice a week with concomitant use of itraconazole, ketoconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole, and clarithromycin;
 reduce dose to 150 mg once daily with concomitant use of fluconazole and erythromycin.
